{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Require all NHS hospitals to provide wards for young people aged 16 to 25",
        "additional_details": "I believe having designated wards could help young people\u2019s mental health as they could provide a place to socialise and engage in activities as well as a room for education and support to prevent them falling behind. It can be scary being admitted to an adult ward when you are a young person and having to advocate for yourself. These wards could help reduce the pressure on young people whilst transitioning to adulthood in other aspects of life.",
        "background": "I want the Government to require dedicated wards to be provided in all NHS hospitals specifically for young people aged 16 to 25. They could make hospital admissions less intimidating and help young people feel less alone and less behind in life compared to others their age.",
